        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF142 Relnote/Expr features: Integrity-Policy can be enforced on styles behind pref]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40747</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40747"/>
        <updated>2025-08-15T03:52:08.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF142 adds support for specifying a style as a blocked destination (behind a preference) in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1974247" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1974247</a>. This updates the release note and experimental features to note that this is an allowed value for the <code class="notranslate">Integrity-Policy</code> and <code class="notranslate">Integrity-Policy-Report-Only</code> headers.</p>
<p dir="auto">Note that I did these as separate entries in relnote and experimental features. I could have done them together perhaps, but they are under different preferences, and may well release separately.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3302143499" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40667" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40667/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40667">#40667</a></p>]]></content>
