        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This change:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>adds the information that clicking an extension suggestion in the address bar (omnibox) is now a user action, including a release note.</li>
<li>adds details of all the user action enabled APIs.</li>
<li>tidies up the content on the user action page.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">In addition to the change requested as part of a dev-doc-needed, the user actions page seemed hard to read and didn't provide a comprehensive guide to the related API's.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1542358" rel="nofollow">Bug 1542358</a> Allow omnibox.onInputEntered as a user action trigger e.g. for clipboard &amp; browserAction.openPopup()</p>]]></content>
